ddressbook><name>IWAMOTO, RYUICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOZAKI, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of regenerating a hydrogenation catalyst characterized by burning a spent hydrogenation catalyst and then subjecting it to a treatment for adherent-metal removal, such as washing with water. Thus, a hydrogenation catalyst for hydrocarbon oils can be effectively regenerated.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Ce procédé de regénération d'un catalyseur d'hydrogénation se caractérise par le brûlage d'un catalyseur d'hydrogénation épuisé. On soumet ensuite ce catalyseur à un traitement visant à éliminer le métal y adhérant, notamment par lavage à l'eau. Ce procédé permet de regénérer de manière satisfaisante un catalyseur d'hydrogénation pour huiles hydrocarbonées.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>